## 7. Rhino sidecar

This dossier ships with a `dossier.3dm` sidecar in the same output folder. Drag it into your Rhino model to drop the following geometry at the site origin (units: meters):

- **Layer `Site`** — site point, address/coords text dot.
- **Layer `Sun_Paths`** — one polyline per key day (summer solstice, winter solstice, equinoxes), traced as sun-vector tips on a 10 m sphere.
- **Layer `Wind_Rose`** — 16 radial spokes scaled to a 20 m base; spoke length is proportional to the share of hours blowing from that sector.
- **Layer `Annotations`** — true-north arrow on +Y, cardinal labels (N/E/S/W).

A `sun_wind_hourly.csv` is also written next to the `.3dm` with Ladybug-compatible columns so you can pipe the raw hourly data into Grasshopper.

